winex11: a core mouse event must carry raw input when there is no XInput2.

Raw mouse input has one producer upstream -- X11DRV_RawMotion and
X11DRV_RawButtonEvent, both XI2 -- and the core paths suppress it with
SEND_HWMSG_NO_RAW. Vessel's X server has no XInput extension, so WM_INPUT was
never posted for a mouse and dinput8 games (Caribbean Legend) could not click.

Third version. The first posted the core event's absolute position as raw
input, and dinput subtracted a cursor the same event had already moved: the
game's cursor drifted off screen. The second (WINE_REVISION 92) sent relative
deltas between core positions -- and was only ever applied to the build tree,
never written back to this file, so the WINE_REVISION 93 rebuild silently
restored the first.

Neither could serve a game that locks the mouse. Positions are clamped to the
screen, so deltas between them stop at the edge: Empyrion's mouse-look turned
about 640 px' worth from the centre and stopped. Vessel's X server now sends
the motion it was asked for, before clamping, as a _VESSEL_RAW_MOTION
ClientMessage to the focused window (com/winlator change 36). This handles it
and posts relative raw motion; once one has arrived, core motion stops
producing raw motion, so nothing doubles. For an X server that sends no such
message, deltas between core positions remain the fallback, now measured from
the SetCursorPos warp target, process-wide, so a game that re-centres every
frame is not measured from where the pointer was before it. Buttons -- wheel
delta included -- always come from the core event.

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
index 60f7cfde3e3..de46a721907 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -1852,8 +1852,15 @@ struct client_message_handler
     void (*handler)(HWND, XClientMessageEvent *); /* corresponding handler function */
 };
 
+/* Vessel: raw mouse motion from the X server. See x11drv_vessel_raw_motion(). */
+static void handle_vessel_raw_motion( HWND hwnd, XClientMessageEvent *event )
+{
+    x11drv_vessel_raw_motion( (int)event->data.l[0], (int)event->data.l[1] );
+}
+
 static const struct client_message_handler client_messages[] =
 {
+    { XATOM__VESSEL_RAW_MOTION, handle_vessel_raw_motion },
     { XATOM_MANAGER,      handle_manager_message },
     { XATOM_WM_PROTOCOLS, handle_wm_protocols },
     { XATOM__XEMBED,      handle_xembed_protocol },
